# §9 E Block-B in expression position (ruling 7)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ENTERS (docs/design/plano-secao9E-closures.md §3 — the one missing product piece):
#   - THE `Block` AST NODE, in `src/parser/ast.tks`. A new `Block { body: []Statement }` variant is
#     APPENDED LAST to `ExprKind`; `parse_atom` (`src/parser/parse_expr.tks`) gains a leading-`{`
#     value-block branch (`parse_block_expr`, reusing `parse_block`) GATED by `allow_struct`, so it
#     never steals the `{` that opens an `if`/`match` scrutinee block. §9 B construction always carries
#     a type prefix (`Name { … }`), so a `{` with no path before it is unambiguously a block.
#   - THE `TBlockExpr` TAST NODE, in `src/checker/tast.tks`. Appended LAST to `TExprKind`;
#     `type_block_expr` (`src/checker/typer.tks`) types the body in a child scope (`type_block`), takes
#     the trailing value's type (`tblock_type`), and rejects a `void`-tailed or DIVERGING block in value
#     position — the same contract `type_if` imposes on an `if`-as-value without an `else`.
#   - THE FULL `TExprKind` WALK ARMS (the "TLambda was added everywhere" pattern), treating a Block-B as
#     an INLINE statement block (NOT a lifted function): `revalidate`, `initanalysis`, `consteval`,
#     `consteval_form`, `comptime_fold` (fold + loop-propagate), `warnings`, `metrics`, `monomorph`,
#     `escape` (mark/count-reads/chain-stats — inline, so its body IS this frame's), `spine`
#     (cells/points-to/unique/borrowed-from), `reachability`, and `codegen` (lift/self-call/opt-collect).
#   - CODEGEN, in `src/codegen/codegen.tks` (`emit_block_expr`): a GNU statement-expression
#     `({ <Ctype> _tk; <stmts…>; _tk = <tail>; _tk; })`, reusing `emit_branch_value` (the if/match
#     value-arm path) so block-local aggregates and defers are handled identically.
#   - NATIVE/LIR, in `src/lir/lower.tks` (`lower_block_expr`): lowers the prefix inline then yields the
#     trailing value's vreg. Block-local bindings are DROPPED at the closing brace (`lenv_prefix`) while
#     an enclosing-scalar reassignment made inside the block — which updates the shared env prefix in
#     place (`lenv_reassign`) — is PRESERVED, so `{ acc = acc + 1; acc }` leaves `acc`'s write visible.
#   - tkb SER/DE, in `src/emit/tkb_write.tks` / `tkb_read.tks` / `tkb_frame.tks`: a new expr tag 26 that
#     round-trips the body as `[]TStatement` (mirroring the IF/MATCH block encoding), with the frame
#     collector interning the body's strings so it round-trips.
# WHAT DOES NOT ENTER: no memory-model change. The §9 E capture semantics are RATIFIED as-is (owner
# E-capture ruling): closures capture by COPY (snapshot); `by_ref` only for `Reference` bindings;
# writing a copy-captured var stays an error. "estilo C#" is read as the SURFACE (a closure closes over
# names of the scope), not C#'s implicit shared-cell (which would need boxing / a closure-lifetime
# borrow-checker, colliding with move-on-return and R4).
#
# INERTNESS ON THE COMPILER CORPUS. The compiler source uses NO bare value-block in expression position
# (its blocks are `if`/`match`/`fn`/loop bodies and §6 bare block STATEMENTS, none of which reach the
# new `parse_atom` branch); the `Block`/`TBlockExpr` variants are appended, shifting no serialized
# ordinal; tag 26 fires only on a Block-B, which the corpus never produces. gen0 (built from THIS
# bootstrap's predecessor) and bin-a emit a byte-identical teko.c — Block-B is inert until USED, and no
# existing `{`-in-expression site changed meaning (the byte-identical fixpoint proves it).
#
# ACCEPT fixture (examples/regressions/block_expr): a Block-B's trailing expression is its value, a
# Block-B nested inside another, a Block-B reading AND writing an enclosing var inline, a Block-B in
# argument position, a Block-B coexisting with a §9 B construction unambiguously, a closure body that is
# itself a Block-B, and a capture-by-copy snapshot — each case names itself and asserts its own value
# (`scenario`), passing identically on the native inline-block lowering and the C GNU statement-expression
# lowering. REJECT fixture (examples/regressions/block_expr_reject): a Block-B ending in an assignment
